# scrapman — Scrap Man's entire conversation, every quest he appears in.
#
# A quests/dialogue/ file: DIALOGUE blocks and NO QUEST block. See docs/reference/QUEST_TEXT_FORMAT.md.
#
# ⚠ THIS FILE OWNS SCRAP MAN'S CONVERSATION. Importing it REGENERATES Dialogue_Scrapman.asset
# wholesale. His old, always-on merchant Sell is deliberately GONE, replaced by the Sell choice on
# NODE start gated  GATE: complete deliver_the_big_blue  — so his shop unlocks only after the player
# finishes the Big Blue arc. This is the owner's decision (2026-08-15). The catalogue itself is
# unchanged: MERCHANT: scrapman sell opens the existing sell-only Merchant_Scrapman.
#
# ⚠ NEW ITEM IDS the owner is building — the import errors until each ItemData.ItemID matches:
# makeshift_vape (shown, then consumed here) and big_blue (delivered, consumed here).
#
# The quests whose beats live in this file:
#   investigate_weird_vape - quests/investigate_weird_vape.quest (stage 0: inspect the vape, name
#                            his price)
#   deliver_the_big_blue   - quests/deliver_the_big_blue.quest   (stage 0: take the Big Blue, reveal
#                            what he knows)
#
# ⚠ TWO PLAYER LINES REMAIN THE OWNER'S TO WRITE, both on NODE start, both marked  [TODO: ]  :
#   - the line that opens his Sell shop (the MERCHANT choice)
#   - his always-available leave line
# The Big Blue hand-over and the three reveal "[Next]" clicks were written in on 2026-08-15.

DIALOGUE scrapman

NODE start
SPEAKER: scrapman
SPEAK: Easy, what you doing 'ere?
# investigate_weird_vape, stage 0 — first meeting. Requires the makeshift vape carried in from
# Check Out the Church, and consumes it: Scrap Man keeps it to look into.
CHOICE Daniel Paul sent me. Can you check this out for him? -> iwv_inspect
GATE: stage investigate_weird_vape 0
ITEM: makeshift_vape x1 consume
# deliver_the_big_blue, stage 0 — bring back the Big Blue. Consumed on delivery. Scrap Man speaks
# first ("Ah, yes, buzzing.").
CHOICE *Hand him the Big Blue* -> dbb_react
GATE: stage deliver_the_big_blue 0
ITEM: big_blue x1 consume
# The Sell shop — unlocked only once the whole Big Blue arc (deliver_the_big_blue) is complete.
# A MERCHANT choice ends the conversation and opens the shop, so it has no  -> . [TODO: ] is the
# owner's: the line that opens his shop.
CHOICE [TODO: ]
GATE: complete deliver_the_big_blue
MERCHANT: scrapman sell
# The always-available way out. [TODO: ] is the owner's leave line.
CHOICE [TODO: ]

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# investigate_weird_vape, stage 0 — Scrap Man eyes the vape and names his price.

NODE iwv_inspect
SPEAKER: scrapman
SPEAK: *Scrap Man inspects the vape.*
CHOICE I found it on a pretty frenzied Neek at the old church. -> iwv_scratch

NODE iwv_scratch
SPEAKER: scrapman
SPEAK: I can help you out, but this back needs scratching first.
CHOICE Go on. -> iwv_bigblue_ask

NODE iwv_bigblue_ask
SPEAKER: scrapman
SPEAK: Big date coming up. Ask Daniel Paul to sort us out a Big Blue.
# Ends the conversation. Stage 0 (TalkTo scrapman) advances to stage 1 on the interact, so the
# objective becomes "ask Daniel about the Big Blue" as the chat closes.
CHOICE Okay.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# deliver_the_big_blue, stage 0 — Scrap Man takes the Big Blue and reveals what he knows.

NODE dbb_react
SPEAKER: scrapman
SPEAK: Ah, yes, buzzing. Can't believe it. You are an absolute legend. Right then... yep, I'll let you know what's going on.
CHOICE Go on then. -> dbb_reveal1

NODE dbb_reveal1
SPEAKER: scrapman
SPEAK: So, Councillor Mosley's been doing a few dodgy dealings. I saw him talking to Ralph and Sanjeet from the Spartans, and he was buying a box of these weird looking vapes.
CHOICE Uh, right. -> dbb_reveal2

NODE dbb_reveal2
SPEAKER: scrapman
SPEAK: The boxes had these weird Chinese letters on. Shanghai and all that jazz. So I assume it's some sort of weird import. I'm guessing that's got something to do with the vapes, because I ain't seen them anywhere else before, and they're the only characters shady enough to get involved with the Chinese at the minute.
CHOICE Fuckin' hell. -> dbb_reveal3

NODE dbb_reveal3
SPEAKER: scrapman
SPEAK: You should hit up that little trap house out in the north. You might get some answers from them, but I dunno. They ain't always there.
# Ends the conversation. Stage 0 (TalkTo scrapman) advances to stage 1 (the report to Daniel) on
# the interact.
CHOICE Yeah, okay. Right, whatever. Sound. I'll go speak to Daniel Paul's.
